<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    WPR.Framework.Xbox - Xbox Live for MANAGED WP8 titles, served by WPR Hub.

    Built as assembly Microsoft.Xbox 255.255.255.255: the identity a WP8 title's C# names (WinRT
    metadata references carry version 255.255.255.255), the same facade trick as
    WPR.Framework.Phone -> Microsoft.Phone. Because it is one of WPR's own assemblies, the runtime
    binds it before looking in a game's install folder, so it also replaces the do-nothing stub
    WinmdStubber wrote into installs made before it existed. No reinstall needed for that.

    41 packages in the library call Microsoft.Xbox from C# (Gravity Guy 2, Bad Piggies, Rayman
    Jungle/Fiesta Run, the Microsoft casual games, Lara Croft Relic Run ...). All 23 copies of
    Microsoft.Xbox.winmd in the library have the same 365-member surface, which this mirrors with
    .NET's WinRT projection applied (DateTime -> DateTimeOffset, IVectorView -> IReadOnlyList,
    HResult -> Exception, EventHandler -> System.EventHandler).

    Behind it is IXboxLiveHost (WPR.Engine.XboxLive), reached through XboxLiveBackend, which
    ApplicationLaunch fills per launch with the same Wp8NativeXboxHost a WP8 native title uses:
    sign-in is the WPR Hub account (or the guest gamertag), achievements go to achievements.db and
    the hub, leaderboards to the hub. Multiplayer, user messages and marketplace fail the way an
    unreachable Xbox Live did.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup Condition=" '$(OS)' != 'Windows_NT' ">
    <CheckEolWorkloads>false</CheckEolWorkloads>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net10.0;net10.0-android</TargetFrameworks>
    <CheckEolWorkloads>false</CheckEolWorkloads>
    <AssemblyName>Microsoft.Xbox</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>Microsoft.Xbox</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyVersion>255.255.255.255</AssemblyVersion>
    <FileVersion>1.0.0.0</FileVersion>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <SupportedOSPlatformVersion Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net10.0-android'">24.0</SupportedOSPlatformVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\WPR.Framework.WinRT\WPR.Framework.WinRT.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="$(SolutionDir)Engine\WPR.Engine.XboxLive\WPR.Engine.XboxLive.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="WPR.SilverlightCompability.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
